# Spell Queller's two abilities, the second for a player who is not its controller. On Bot2's turn 2 Bot2 Bolts Bot1;
# Bot1 flashes Spell Queller in (CR 702.8a) and its enters ability exiles the Bolt, an opponent's noncreature spell of mana
# value 1: Bot1 takes no damage. On turn 4 Bot2's second Bolt kills the Queller, and its leaves-the-battlefield ability has
# the exiled card's owner, Bot2, cast it as the ability resolves (CR 608.2g, the 2025-01-24 ruling) without paying its mana
# cost (CR 118.9): Bot2 accepts, chooses a new target as it casts it (Bot1's Llanowar Elves, not Bot1 as before: the new
# spell has no relation to the first, the ruling), and pays nothing - its pool stays empty and its second Mountain untapped.
# The Bolt is Bot2's spell (CR 405.4): it kills the Elves and goes to Bot2's graveyard.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Llanowar Elves
Spell Queller
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain x2
Lightning Bolt x2
Island x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Spell Queller.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Exile = Lightning Bolt
? Stack.Count = 0
? Bot1.Life = 20
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain#1.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Spell Queller)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Accept
Bot2.Target(Llanowar Elves)
? Stack = Lightning Bolt
? Bot2.Mana = 
[Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot1.Graveyard = Llanowar Elves; Spell Queller
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt; Lightning Bolt
Exile.Count = 0
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain#1.Tapped = true
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain#2.Tapped = false
